Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turn the read-only dashboard into a control plane over the configurable
workflow architecture, with copy-as-command as the Tier-1 write path (the
dashboard is a static file:// SPA — no server).

Snapshot bake (generate-snapshot.mjs): new snapshot.workflow — resolved runtime
graph (phases/roles/gates/rails/evidence/artifacts/plan sub-skills/edges), raw
.forge/config.yaml via loadRawConfig (absent = all-defaults), PROFILES, a skills
catalog (precedence + skills-lock hash/source + per-harness SessionStart matrix),
and lintRuntimeGraphConfig warnings.

Cockpit view (app.js): a top-level Workflow view, one SECTION PER SURFACE —
6-stage chain rail (role→skill + gates/evidence/artifacts + plan's 5 sub-skills),
gates panel (4 stage + 3 human + issue_verify, locked greyed + why), rails (locked
except kernel_tracking), skills catalog, profiles×stage matrix (read-only SEAM),
plus reserved follow-up placeholders for Hooks/MCP/Rules and a tri-state
control-state note (mandatory/optional/permission). Honesty badges throughout.

Copy-as-command on every configurable item: forge gate disable/enable <id> and
forge role <stage> --use <skill>, via the DataSource seam (Tier-2 server drops in
without render changes).

Honest SEAM: review/verify are roles only — the graph exposes phase records for
plan/dev/validate/ship; their gates/evidence are not faked.

